gapClasses.fix:
One walk-time compile budget in bytes, refused with RZ-CFG-005 where it is crossed, computed incrementally without building strings. It counts:
(a) every value of every subschema keyword, at its pointer length as the library spells it;
(b) every position's location bytes times the equal-length queued entries (or a per-position cap);
(c) every reference's base + value + resolved target pointer;
(d) every resource's resolved $id length times (resources + positions).
Also:
- the walk refuses non-schema values at subschema positions, with the meta-schema's message, before the library collects them;
- WP-51 builds pointer strings only for reported findings (checkNumbers, eachSubschema, stringEntries, metaIssues capped at MaxIssues), keeps parent indexes, parses each base URL once, dedupes w.targets, and compares pointers without rescanning decimals.
The limit is an owner decision (ordinary 4,096-position schemas use about 0.25 to 0.5 MB), with a contract request against 07 req 75 and R-77.

