gapClasses.class:
GC-21. Format assertion reaches request bodies on library-only routes, and the asserted format 'regex' calls WP-51's compile-time regexp cache at request time.
The route in:
- the library asserts format when the resource's dialect has the format-assertion vocabulary (objcompiler.go:436-445);
- a library-only resource's $schema can give it that dialect: the bundled meta/format-assertion, or policy.json with a root $vocabulary;
- recordOnce applies only at walked positions, and the inspector checks only DraftVersion (inspect.go:169-171).
The mechanism: Format.Validate for 'regex' is roots.regexpEngine.validate (objcompiler.go:188-192), bound to regexpCache.compile (schema.go:383-403), an unlocked map that every compiled Schema keeps and that is called once per body string (validator.go:136-142).
The effects:
- a fatal concurrent map write (CC-01, confirmed again at finalize);
- kept memory that grows without bound (CC-02);
- uncharged request-time work (CC-03);
- format asserted on bodies, and sibling keywords dropped (CC-04).
VLU-41, CMP-58, VAL-13, CX-28 and VAL-68 claimed otherwise and are reclassified as partial.

